          "text": "HELLO",
          "frames": 2500,
          "expect": ["Hi, sailor. New in town?"]
        }
      ],
      "notes": "End to end: C compiles HELLO.C to HELLO.ASM, AS assembles it to HELLO.COM and the program prints 'Hi, sailor. New in town?'.  Two staging rules.  The compiler #includes its library *source* at compile time, so PRINTF.C has to be on the disk or the compile stops with \"Can't find file\"; the fixture therefore starts with #include \"printf.c\" (the repo's plain HELLO.C compiles but assembles with an undefined printf).  And AS needs CLIBRARY.ASM, not just CLIBRARY.REL: it opens the .ASM to pull in the library.  The .REL files are not needed at all.  This is a fifth C toolchain alongside Aztec, BDS and the BASIC/FORTRAN/Pascal families, and it targets 8080 rather than Z80 code."
